{
  "assembly_notes": "One carcass part carries the body shell, the support base, the face frame and the shelf ladder; every door leaf is a separate moving part. The host body always derives a planar front jamb (a chord frame on the curved drum, the narrow top width on the tapered case) so any front treatment and any mechanism mounts on a real supporting face. Leaf width, height, hinge line, track planes and interior swing limits are derived from the opening and from N; no combination is excluded and no overlap allowance is emitted.",
